## 6. Combining CSS Properties in a Practical Example

### HTML

```html
<div class="container">
    <h2>My Learning Journey</h2>

    <ul>
        <li>HTML Basics</li>
        <li>CSS Styling</li>
        <li>Flexbox Layout</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        I am learning frontend development
        and improving my CSS skills every day.
    </p>
</div>
```

### CSS

```css
.container {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;

    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    color: darkblue;
    text-align: center;
}

ul {
    list-style-type: none;
    list-style-position: inside;
}

p {
    text-indent: 50px;
    text-transform: capitalize;
}
```

This example combines Flexbox, text styling, list styling, and inherited properties in one layout.

